{"team":"JAX","col":"#19D3C5","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":60.5,"adot":8.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>No Fixed Address</h2><p>JAX throw by design. They pass <strong>-1%</strong> over expectation (league -2%) and keep firing even with a lead (43% early-down pass when ahead vs ~41%) \u2014 the kind of pass-first identity that keeps receivers live in every script.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 60% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>They push it downfield \u2014 average depth of target <strong>8.6 yards</strong> with 22% of throws traveling 15+, a vertical passing game that trades completions for boom-or-bust yardage.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>48%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Chris Rodriguez Jr.</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 68 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 44 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>109 rushing</strong> and <strong>252 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.31/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB